1 00:00:00,490 --> 00:00:06,330 Imagine the father of evolution, Charles Darwin, sitting in a dimly lit room in 2025. 2 00:00:07,130 --> 00:09,10 He has spent his entire life studying the slow methodical process of natural 3 00:09,10 --> 00:19,170 selection, observing the beak shapes of finches and the shell patterns of tortoise to understand how life survives. 4 00:19,650 --> 00:21,190 He is a man of patience. 5 00:21,680 --> 00:24,750 He is a man of rigorous scientific observation. 6 00:25,120 --> 00:32,590 And now we have handed him an iPhone 17, unlocked it and opened a terrifying application called Tinder. 7 00:33,180 --> 00:38,470 He is about to witness the modern struggle for existence and he is absolutely terrified. 8 00:39,830 --> 00:46,60 To understand Darwin's confusion, you have to remember that in the Victorian era, courtship was a marathon. 9 00:46,550 --> 00:55,770 It involved handwritten letters, supervised walks in the garden and checking the size of a woman's dowry to ensure distinct survival advantages for your offspring. 10 00:56,230 --> 00:57,80 It was slow. 11 00:57,690 --> 00:58,690 It was deliberate. 12 00:59,100 --> 01:07,130 Now, Darwin is looking at a screen where potential mates are discarded with a flick of the thumb faster than a chameleon strikes a fly. 13 01:07,670 --> 01:10,240 He asks what the swiping motion represents. 14 01:10,740 --> 01:15,820 We explained that left means extinction and right means potential breeding partner. 15 01:16,240 --> 01:17,670 His eyes go wide. 16 01:17,990 --> 01:21,870 He realizes he is looking at the most ruthless environment on earth. 17 01:22,460 --> 01:28,870 He adjusts his spectacles, clears his throat and begins his analysis of the North American horned single. 18 01:30,220 --> 01:34,310 The first profile appears, it is a man named Kyle, age 27. 19 01:35,30 --> 01:37,840 Kyle's first photo is a mirror selfie in a gymnasium. 20 01:37,840 --> 01:46,260 He is flexing his bicep to an unnatural degree, his face turning a shade of crimson that in nature usually indicates toxicity. 21 01:46,900 --> 01:48,150 Darwin is fascinated. 22 01:48,590 --> 01:50,600 He leans in, squinting at the screen. 23 01:51,50 --> 01:56,210 He notes that this male is displaying hypertrophy, an excessive growth of muscle mass. 24 01:56,660 --> 02:0,870 In the wild, this would be useful for fighting off rivals or hunting large game. 25 02:1,220 --> 02:5,940 However, Darwin scrolls down and sees Kyle's job title is social media manager. 26 02:6,550 --> 02:7,750 Darwin is confused. 27 02:7,970 --> 02:12,630 Why does a man who sits at a desk require the trappings of a silverback gorilla? 28 02:13,220 --> 02:23,800 He concludes that these muscles are purely ornamental, much like the tail of a peacock, cumbersome, useless for survival, but necessary to attract a mate who values heavy lifting. 29 02:24,250 --> 02:31,560 Darwin swipes left, murdering that the energy expenditure required to maintain those pectorals is an inefficient use of calories. 30 02:32,320 --> 02:35,10 The next profile is a woman named Tiffany. 31 02:35,420 --> 02:42,500 Her photos are confusing, in every single one, she has the ears of a dog and a nose that disappears into a blur of light. 32 02:43,210 --> 02:44,240 Darwin panics. 33 02:44,570 --> 02:49,430 Has the human species hybridized with canines, is this a new evolutionary branch? 34 02:50,170 --> 02:51,690 We explain it is a filter. 35 02:52,100 --> 02:53,420 Darwin is appalled. 36 02:53,960 --> 02:57,590 In nature, this is called mimicry, it is a biological lie. 37 02:58,90 --> 03:3,750 It is the equivalent of a harmless fly painting itself yellow and black to look like a dangerous wasp. 38 03:4,320 --> 03:7,840 He argues that this disrupts the integrity of sexual selection. 39 03:7,840 --> 03:12,710 If you cannot see the mate's true phenotype, how can you assess their genetic fitness? 40 03:13,170 --> 03:14,230 He reads her bio. 41 03:14,230 --> 03:19,20 It says, "If you can't handle me at my worst, you don't deserve me at my best." 42 03:19,340 --> 03:20,530 Darwin's size. 43 03:20,950 --> 03:28,20 He notes that in nature, if an animal is at its worst, say a slow gazelle or a sick lion, it simply gets eaten. 44 03:28,490 --> 03:29,970 There is no deserving. 45 03:30,170 --> 03:31,480 There is only survival. 46 03:31,880 --> 03:32,840 He swipes left. 47 03:33,520 --> 03:38,720 Then the algorithm feeds him the most common specimen of all, the guy holding a fish. 48 03:39,410 --> 03:40,430 Darwin pauses. 49 03:40,780 --> 03:43,150 He has seen this display in hundreds of profiles. 50 03:43,620 --> 03:46,810 A male grinning, holding a dead bass towards the camera. 51 03:47,430 --> 03:48,600 Darwin nods slowly. 52 03:49,150 --> 03:50,810 Finally, something that makes sense. 53 03:51,260 --> 03:53,50 This is a classic provider signal. 54 03:53,470 --> 03:56,580 The male is demonstrating his ability to secure resources. 55 03:56,980 --> 04:1,360 He's showing the female that if they mate, he can provide protein for the offspring. 56 04:1,740 --> 04:3,160 But then Darwin looks closer. 57 04:3,550 --> 04:4,480 The fish is small. 58 04:4,740 --> 04:5,900 It is barely a snack. 59 04:6,410 --> 04:12,880 He calculates that this fish provides perhaps 200 calories, hardly enough to sustain a family through a harsh winter. 60 04:13,760 --> 04:20,440 Furthermore, the male is wearing sunglasses indoors, which suggests poor vision or a lack of situational awareness. 61 04:20,830 --> 04:25,480 Darwin concludes that while the hunting instinct is present, the execution is flawed. 62 04:25,970 --> 04:31,430 He notes that a true provider would display a harvested deer or perhaps a large sack of grain. 63 04:31,730 --> 04:34,800 He swipes left, disappointed by the caloric inefficiency. 64 04:35,840 --> 04:38,300 Darwin discovers the height requirement in bios. 65 04:38,770 --> 04:42,750 He sees profile after profile stating 6-foot or swipe left. 66 04:43,260 --> 04:46,140 He is astounded by this brutal sexual dimorphism. 67 04:46,650 --> 04:52,650 In the animal kingdom, size often dictates dominance, yes, but this level of specificity is unprecedented. 68 04:53,300 --> 04:58,630 He reads a bio from a man named Brad that says, "5'11, but I lie and say six. 69 04:59,100 --> 05:0,40 Darwin chuckles. 70 05:0,410 --> 05:2,780 This is a fascinating behavioral adaptation. 71 05:3,260 --> 05:11,590 It's a deceptive signaling strategy, similar to a crab growing one massive claw to intimidate rivals, even if the claw is weak and hollow. 72 05:12,170 --> 05:17,890 He respects the hustle but questions the long-term viability of a relationship built on a geometric falsehood. 73 05:18,740 --> 05:20,600 He moves on to the traveler archetype. 74 05:21,50 --> 05:26,90 The woman standing on a cliff in Bali, the man posing with a sedated tiger in Thailand. 75 05:26,600 --> 05:30,240 He reads the bio, "Wanderlust, not looking for anything serious." 76 05:30,780 --> 05:33,180 He identifies this as a migratory species. 77 05:33,750 --> 05:42,320 In biology, migration is usually driven by seasonal changes or food scarcity, but these humans seem to migrate purely for the sake of content. 78 05:42,700 --> 05:44,520 He is confused by the tiger photo. 79 05:44,910 --> 05:47,750 Why would a primate cuddle with an apex predator? 80 05:48,110 --> 05:52,910 It goes against every survival instinct encoded in our DNA over millions of years. 81 05:53,230 --> 05:57,20 He realizes that natural selection has stopped working on these people. 82 05:57,710 --> 06:2,710 In the Pleistocene era, the man hugging the tiger would be removed from the gene pool immediately. 83 06:3,160 --> 06:5,470 In 2026, he gets a match. 84 06:5,940 --> 06:7,890 Darwin finds this deeply disturbing. 85 06:8,530 --> 06:10,360 Then comes the crypto bro. 86 06:10,870 --> 06:14,480 The bio reads, "Entrepreneur, crypto enthusiast, to the moon." 87 06:15,100 --> 06:16,610 Darwin asks what crypto is. 88 06:17,40 --> 06:23,710 We explained it is a currency that doesn't exist physically, based on solving math problems to buy pictures of bored monkeys. 89 06:24,140 --> 06:25,970 Darwin puts his head in his hands. 90 06:26,380 --> 06:31,340 He spent his life studying tangible reality, fossils, bones, seeds. 91 06:31,650 --> 06:36,250 The idea that resources are now imaginary concepts breaks his Victorian brain. 92 06:36,920 --> 06:46,20 He theorizes that this is a form of runaway selection where a trait becomes desirable not because it is useful but simply because the females think it is useful. 93 06:46,550 --> 06:47,560 It's a bubble. 94 06:47,790 --> 06:56,120 He predicts that when the environmental conditions change, say the power goes out, the crypto bro will have zero survival value compared to the guy holding the fish. 95 06:56,660 --> 07:0,870 For the first time, Darwin feels a new found respect for the fish guy. 96 07:1,200 --> 07:4,180 At least you can eat a bass, you cannot eat a Bitcoin. 97 07:4,930 --> 07:9,70 He stumbles upon the poly and ethical non-monogamy section of Tinder. 98 07:9,460 --> 07:12,790 He reads a bio, married, dating separately, looking for a third. 99 07:13,290 --> 07:14,880 Darwin is fascinated. 100 07:15,220 --> 07:16,360 He pulls out his notebook. 101 07:16,690 --> 07:20,590 He compares this to the mating habits of bonobos or certain flocking birds. 102 07:20,950 --> 07:26,590 He notes that while monogamy is common in humans, this open strategy increases genetic diversity. 103 07:27,150 --> 07:29,230 However, he is baffled by the logistics. 104 07:29,660 --> 07:32,670 He reads about Google calendars and scheduling conflicts. 105 07:33,10 --> 07:39,110 He observes that the energy required to maintain multiple mates seems to outweigh the reproductive benefits. 106 07:39,470 --> 07:45,430 He watches a user try to schedule a date with three different people, fail, and end up eating pizza alone. 107 07:45,910 --> 07:50,600 Darwin writes down, "social complexity has exceeded the organism's carrying capacity." 108 07:51,520 --> 07:54,770 Suddenly, the app tells Darwin that he has a super like. 109 07:55,100 --> 07:56,690 He panics, is this a predator? 110 07:57,110 --> 07:59,380 No, it is a signal of high interest. 111 07:59,970 --> 08:1,330 He looks at the profile. 112 08:1,590 --> 08:2,240 It is a bot. 113 08:2,490 --> 08:6,490 It is a computer program pretending to be a 20-year-old model named Glof. 114 08:7,40 --> 08:8,210 Darwin engages with it. 115 08:8,420 --> 08:11,100 The bot sends a link to a suspicious webcam site. 116 08:11,540 --> 08:15,640 Darwin, innocent and naive, clicks it, thinking it is a scientific journal. 117 08:16,100 --> 08:18,500 His phone is immediately infected with malware. 118 08:18,970 --> 08:22,80 The screen flashes, Darwin throws the phone across the room. 119 08:22,540 --> 08:27,890 He assumes the device has contracted a virus, which is technically true, though he's thinking of smallpox. 120 08:28,600 --> 08:32,490 He retrieves the phone and decides to look at the bio section one last time. 121 08:32,940 --> 08:35,110 He sees the phrase sapiosexual. 122 08:35,530 --> 08:38,400 We explain this means being attracted to intelligence. 123 08:38,870 --> 08:40,20 Darwin perks up. 124 08:40,320 --> 08:42,880 Finally, a selection pressure he can get behind. 125 08:43,260 --> 08:50,810 He imagines these people are looking for partners who can quote Lyle's distinct principles of geology or discuss the classification of barnacles. 126 08:51,260 --> 08:52,650 He swipes right, he matches. 127 08:53,160 --> 08:59,860 He sends a message, "Dearest madam, what are your thoughts on the transmutation of species regarding the Galapagos finches?" 128 09:00,310 --> 09:1,590 The reply comes instantly. 129 09:1,930 --> 09:4,310 Lol, you talk weird, you want some fuck? 130 09:4,800 --> 09:6,300 Darwin stares at the screen. 131 09:6,760 --> 09:10,20 The degradation of language is more rapid than he anticipated. 132 09:10,500 --> 09:18,480 He realizes that intelligence in 2025 doesn't mean scientific literacy, it means knowing how to use emojis without looking like a boomer. 133 09:19,160 --> 09:21,500 As the day ends, Darwin sets the phone down. 134 09:21,980 --> 09:23,100 He looks weary. 135 09:23,380 --> 09:27,50 He has witnessed the future of his species and the data is concerning. 136 09:27,520 --> 09:31,990 He has seen males prening like birds of paradise without the ability to build a nest. 137 09:32,290 --> 09:36,360 He has seen females applying digital camouflage to hide their true form. 138 09:36,700 --> 09:47,730 He has seen a total disconnect between fitness in the biological sense, health, strength, adaptability, and fitness in the Tinder sense, gym selfies and Instagram follower counts. 139 09:48,250 --> 09:55,750 He concludes that sexual selection in 2026 is no longer about survival of the fittest, it's survival of the thirstiest. 140 09:56,120 --> 10:4,680 The traits being selected for, vanity, deception, and the ability to take a photo from a high angle, offer no advantage in the struggle against the elements. 141 10:5,270 --> 10:10,580 If a meteor were to strike tomorrow, the influencers and the crypto bros would be the first to perish. 142 10:11,50 --> 10:16,770 The future belongs to the quiet, the practical, perhaps even the ones holding the small, sad fish. 143 10:17,460 --> 10:21,890 Darwin stands up, adjusts his coat, and decides to go back to his earthworms. 144 10:22,190 --> 10:31,80 They are slimy, they are blind, and they live in dirt, but at least they don't ghost you after three weeks of talking because they aren't ready for something serious right now. 145 10:31,390 --> 10:40,730 He walks out the door, leaving the phone buzzing on the table with a new notification, it's a match, but Charles Darwin has already evolved beyond the need for swiping. 146 10:41,400 --> 10:42,980 The human race is fascinating, he thinks. 147 10:43,450 --> 10:46,650 But frankly, the barnacles were much less complicated.